From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronan Abhamon <ronan.abhamon@vates.tech>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:58:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: keep CBT log / secondary at right position

A CBT log is added first by these calls: `open -C`, `unpause -c`, ...
There are a few places where this behavior is broken and where log files
are altered:
- The `ENOSPC` failover of `tapdisk_vbd_complete_td_request` would, in
  mirror mode, retire the log instead of the leaf, and, in standby
  mode, insert the secondary image above the log (the writes would no
  longer be logged).
- Using local cache with `tap-ctl create -r -C <log> -a vhd:<child of a VHD chain>`,
  a write through the device fails (`EOPNOTSUPP`) and is lost.
- `tapdisk_vbd_add_secondary` inserts the secondary image (`-2`) right
  after the log: log -> secondary -> leaf -> parents.
  We want this instead: log -> leaf -> secondary -> parents. Otherwise
  the write calls are only received by the secondary and the leaf
  is never modified...

Signed-off-by: Ronan Abhamon <ronan.abhamon@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c b/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
index b66825ae..13a544c4 100644
--- a/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
+++ b/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
@@ -376,7 +376,7 @@ tapdisk_vbd_add_local_cache(td_vbd_t *vbd)
 	td_image_t *cache, *parent;
 	int err;
 
-	parent = tapdisk_vbd_first_image(vbd);
+	parent = tapdisk_vbd_first_non_log_image(vbd);
 	if (tapdisk_vbd_is_last_image(vbd, parent)) {
 		DPRINTF("Single-image chain, nothing to cache");
 		return 0;
@@ -442,7 +442,7 @@ tapdisk_vbd_add_secondary(td_vbd_t *vbd)
 	if (type < 0)
 		return type;
 
-	leaf = tapdisk_vbd_first_image(vbd);
+	leaf = tapdisk_vbd_first_non_log_image(vbd);
 	if (!leaf) {
 		err = -EINVAL;
 		goto fail;
@@ -1632,7 +1632,7 @@ tapdisk_vbd_complete_td_request(td_request_t treq, int res)
 	if (abs(res) == ENOSPC && td_flag_test(image->flags,
 				TD_IGNORE_ENOSPC)) {
 		res = 0;
-		leaf = tapdisk_vbd_first_image(vbd);
+		leaf = tapdisk_vbd_first_non_log_image(vbd);
 		if (vbd->secondary_mode == TD_VBD_SECONDARY_MIRROR) {
 			DPRINTF("ENOSPC: disabling mirroring\n");
 			list_del_init(&leaf->next);
